{
  id:"pt-tabes-dorsalis", title:"Tabes dorsalis (neurosyphilis): sensory ataxia and physiotherapy", subject:"Neurology", region:"Spinal cord (dorsal columns)", stages:"012344",
  aliases:["locomotor ataxia","neurosyphilis","sensory ataxia","Charcot joint","Frenkel's exercises","Argyll Robertson pupil"],
  simple:"Tabes dorsalis is a late form of untreated syphilis in which the dorsal roots and dorsal columns of the spinal cord degenerate. The patient loses position sense in the legs, so they walk on a wide base, stamping their feet and watching the ground, and fall in the dark. Physiotherapy uses Frenkel's exercises, vision and safe aids to rebuild controlled walking.",
  flow:["Untreated syphilis (Treponema pallidum) for 10-30 years","Degeneration of dorsal roots and dorsal columns","Lightning pains, sensory ataxia, areflexia, Romberg positive","Serology, CSF VDRL, sensory and gait testing","Penicillin; PT: Frenkel's, balance, gait aids, joint protection","Prevent falls, Charcot joints and bladder complications"],
  exam:[
    {h:"Definition and pathology", p:["A form of tertiary neurosyphilis affecting dorsal roots (especially lumbosacral) and posterior columns of the spinal cord.","Demyelination and atrophy of posterior columns (fasciculus gracilis more than cuneatus); dorsal root ganglia involved.","Now rare after penicillin but still seen, especially with HIV co-infection."]},
    {h:"Clinical features", p:["Lightning pains: sudden stabbing pains in the legs; visceral crises (gastric).","Sensory ataxia: wide-based, high-stepping, stamping gait, watching the feet; worse in the dark; Romberg sign positive.","Loss of vibration and joint position sense, deep pain loss (painless pressure on Achilles tendon - Abadie's sign), areflexia, hypotonia, flexor plantars.","Argyll Robertson pupils (small, irregular, accommodate but do not react to light), ptosis, optic atrophy.","Charcot (neuropathic) joints in knees and hips; atonic bladder with overflow; trophic ulcers."]},
    {h:"Investigations", p:["Serum VDRL or RPR and treponemal tests (TPHA, FTA-ABS); CSF VDRL, raised cells and protein.","X-ray of joints for Charcot changes; urodynamics for bladder; HIV testing."]},
    {h:"Physiotherapy management", p:["Frenkel's exercises: slow, precise, repeated movements with full visual attention, progressing lying, sitting, standing, walking; each movement 3-4 times per session, sessions several times a day (often every 3-4 hours), short to avoid fatigue.","Gait training: walking on floor markings or footprints, turning practice, use of mirror; wide-based stick or walker; good lighting at home and a night light.","Balance training with visual feedback, progressing to reduced vision cautiously; weight bearing and approximation for proprioceptive input; weighted cuffs (about 0.5-1 kg) may help some patients.","Joint protection for Charcot joints: knee braces or calipers, avoid high impact; protect anaesthetic feet with footwear and daily skin checks.","Bladder training with timed voiding or CIC as advised; pain management for lightning pains (medical plus TENS as an adjunct)."]},
    {h:"Prognosis and conclusion", p:["Penicillin halts progression but rarely reverses established loss; therapy aims to use vision to compensate for lost proprioception and keep the patient safe and walking.","Frenkel's exercises are the classic answer and are still used for any sensory ataxia (B12 deficiency, neuropathy)."]}
  ],
  tip:"Draw a spinal cord cross-section with the posterior columns and dorsal roots shaded, labelled 'degenerated'. Beside it draw a man walking with a wide base, watching his feet, and a Frenkel's footprint ladder on the floor.",
  evidence:[["Frenkel's exercises for sensory ataxia","Clinically used; limited controlled evidence","Low"],["Penicillin for neurosyphilis","Halts disease progression","High"]],
  evidenceSource:"Cash's Textbook of Neurology; CDC sexually transmitted infections treatment guidelines (2021)",
  outcomes:[["Romberg test","Proprioceptive dependence on vision"],["Berg Balance Scale","Balance and fall risk"],["10-metre walk test","Gait speed"],["Joint position sense testing","Proprioception"]],
  recent:["Syphilis rates have risen globally in the last decade, so neurosyphilis is again included in the differential of sensory ataxia, particularly with HIV."],
  mnemonic:{word:"TABES", items:[["T","Tingling and lightning pains"],["A","Ataxia (sensory), Argyll Robertson pupils, areflexia"],["B","Bladder (atonic)"],["E","Eyes closed falls (Romberg positive)"],["S","Stamping gait, sensory loss, Charcot joints"]], extra:"Frenkel's = slow, precise, visually guided repetition."},
  example:"A 58-year-old lorry driver from Salem stamps his feet and falls when the power goes off at night. Serology confirms neurosyphilis; after penicillin, the physio teaches Frenkel's exercises with floor footprints, a walking stick and a night lamp.",
  flags:["Painless swollen unstable joint (Charcot joint)","Retention with overflow and recurrent UTI","Falls in darkness or on uneven ground"],
  viva:[["Which tracts are affected in tabes dorsalis?","Dorsal roots and posterior (dorsal) columns."],["Romberg sign in tabes?","Positive: falls or sways with eyes closed."],["Principle of Frenkel's exercises?","Use vision and concentration to replace lost proprioception through slow, precise repetition."]],
  refs:[{b:"cashNeuro",ch:"Disorders of sensation; Frenkel's exercises"},{b:"osullivan",ch:"Coordination examination and interventions"},{c:"Workowski KA, et al. Sexually Transmitted Infections Treatment Guidelines, 2021. MMWR Recommendations and Reports. 2021.", q:"Workowski sexually transmitted infections treatment guidelines 2021 MMWR"}],
  keywords:"tabes dorsalis neurosyphilis sensory ataxia dorsal column Romberg Argyll Robertson Charcot joint Frenkel's exercises lightning pains",
  mcq:[["Argyll Robertson pupil reacts to:",["Light but not accommodation","Accommodation but not light","Neither","Both normally"],1,"It accommodates but does not react to light."],["The main exercise approach for sensory ataxia in tabes dorsalis is:",["PNF only","Frenkel's exercises","Rood brushing","Interferential therapy"],1,"Frenkel's exercises use vision to compensate for lost proprioception."]]
}
